        "name": "Vishnu Sahasranama",
        "description": "Vishnu Sahasranama is one of the most sacred and powerful hymns in Hindu tradition, containing 1000 names of Lord Vishnu. Composed by Sage Vyasa and recited by Bhishma to Yudhishthira on the battlefield of Kurukshetra, this hymn describes the infinite qualities, forms, and glories of Lord Vishnu. Each name reveals a different aspect of the Supreme Being - from His cosmic form to His intimate presence in every atom of creation. The recitation of Vishnu Sahasranama is believed to purify the mind, remove all obstacles, and grant liberation to the sincere devotee. The hymn is structured in poetic meter and is divided into several sections, each focusing on different attributes of the divine.",
